    "zonal_office address comes only from the relief-centre legend of the map on p.382 (R2, ward 53); no office phone is printed. No hospital/UPHC list, police or fire contacts are given in this zone's appendix.",
    "Assistant Executive Engineer 'Addl. AEE' and Sanitary Officer for wards 49 to 53 are printed as 'Vacant' (no phone).",
    "CMWSSB contact (p.367) is printed as 'Area Engineer-5 8144930905 Asst. Engineer-49 to 63 8144930049 to 8144930063'. Only the Area Engineer number is stored as a phone; the Assistant Engineer per-ward numbers are given only as that range and were not expanded.",
    "Divisional Engineer (HQ) phone printed as '9445190751 & 753'; the second number is recorded as 9445190753 (same 7-digit prefix). NDRF Commandant phone printed as '04177 – 246594/246269'; second number recorded with the shared 04177 prefix.",
    "Conservancy supervisor is printed 'Conservany supervisor' (kept). The p.367 contact table repeats the three ward-range supervisors with area names (Royapuram/Harbour/Egmore), merged into the wards field.",
    "inundation_streets = 'Water stagnated streets in the previous monsoon - heavy rain' table (p.372, 13 rows); no depth/days columns. Disposal point is blank in the source for rows 7 (VOC Salai) and 10 (Singanna Chetty Street). Trailing commas after street names dropped. Text says 13 spots.",
    "Mild-rain table (p.377) has a single row with ward '49 to 63'.",
    "Sewer-block table (pp.378-379) also gives 'No. of manholes' per street (total 154), not captured by the schema.",
    "Relief centres: text says 11 centres / capacity 2250 but the table (pp.379-381) has 10 rows. Facility columns are ordered Drinking water | Toilets | Cooking facilities (verified on the page image); every row reads Yes | Yes | NO, i.e. cooking = false. Several 'Name & Address' cells list two or three venues run together (rows 3-8); kept as one entry per row as printed. Rows 6-8 have no streets listed. Contact designations are printed as SI / AE / ARO; the Responsibilities column is added in brackets.",
    "The relief/evacuation map (p.382, labels omitted in the text file) carries a DIFFERENT legend, not used for the arrays: R1 50 Community Hall at Shaik Mastiry Street; R2 53 Zonal office-5, No:61, Basin Bridge Road, Royapuram; R3 58 Coummunity Hall Kannapar thidal Sydenhams Road; R4 59 Coummunity Hall, SMNager; R5 62 MRTS Railway Station Chinthardripet; R6 61 Anthoneyar School Adithanar Salai, Egmore; R7 61 Chennai Middle School, Varatharaja Puram, Egmore; R8 62 Chennai High School,West Coovum Road, Pudupet; R9 62 Corporation Gym, Ulagappa Street Chinthadripet; R10 63 Chennai Primary School, Goyathoppu Street, Pudupet; R11 63 Veerapatheran Street Coummunity Hall, Pudupet. Streets to be shifted (E1-E11): 50 Corporation Colony; 53 Chidambaram Nagar; 58 Thideer Nagar and Natesan Nagar; 59 Gandhi Nagar; 59 Pallavan Nagar; 61 Transport Lane; 61 Varatharajapuram; 62 Rex Street, Five huts; 62 West Coovum road; 63 South Coovum road; 63 Boothaperumal koil street. (Read from the page image.)",
    "Streets that require evacuation: the source states there was no evacuation in Royapuram zone in 2015, so evacuation_streets is empty.",
    "Water-entered-houses (p.385): one row, ward 53 ('Dr.Vijaya Rahavalu Road'), whose cell lists 6 streets; split into 6 entries (text says 6 locations).",
    "Tree fall (p.385): each ward cell lists several locations on separate lines; split into 13 entries (text says 13).",
    "Rescue boats: source says no rescue boats were needed in this zone. Only one NDRF location is given.",
    "Parks (p.365): text says 25 parks but 26 rows are listed. 'Name / Location' split at the first comma into name and location; row 26 location is truncated in the source ('D’').",
    "Pumping stations (p.366): ward not given; all 9 are 30 MLD. Two-line names joined with a comma.",
    "The zone text ends partway through 'Transport Equipments & Lorries' (p.386); the lorry table is not in the file."
